<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Partial contact: half the interface lifts off under an eccentric load</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-05</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>no</isVerified>
    <description>
      The ContactPatchTest3d cubes and support, but the pressure on the top face is linear in x,
      p = 1e6*(1 + 2*x), so it carries a moment as well as a net force. A contact interface
      cannot pull, so the windward half opens and the load is carried by the remaining half.

      This is the first testcase whose active set actually CHANGES during the Newton solve: it
      goes 11 -> 8 and then settles, which makes it the regression test for the per-iteration
      active-set diagnostic and the chattering warning.

      The check that does not depend on any of that is equilibrium: whatever lifts off, the
      interface is still the only load path to the support, so the resultant contact force must
      equal the applied one exactly, 1e6 * 4 = 4e6 N.

      integrationOrder is raised to 6 (4x4 points per segment) on purpose. At the default order
      the interface has only 2x2 points, and once a column of them opens the two that remain lie
      on one line: the upper body can then rotate about it freely, the tangent is rank
      deficient, and the solve diverges.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactPartialLiftoff3d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="3d">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="3d">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="cube_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="6"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body fully supported -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/><comp dof="z"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- upper body: suppress the lateral rigid-body modes only. Its z support comes
               exclusively from the contact interface, which is the point of the test. -->
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- linear in x: net force 1e6*4 plus a moment, so part of the interface opens -->
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6*(1+2*x)"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
